Based on the report and your screenshot, the problem is that when you render inline content (for example a `<span>…</span>`) inside the Overlay, the wrapper never gets any intrinsic width and “collapses” to zero.  By default we only set `display:''` on the `.next-overlay-wrapper`, so the browser has no width to render inline content.  The simplest fix is to give the wrapper a `width:100%`, which ensures that it will always span its container and allow inline children to layout properly.

Below is a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch in `src/overlay/overlay.jsx` to add `width: '100%'` to the default `newWrapperStyle`.  

```javascript
